<PlatformLayout title="Kéire Hub for Windows" description="Get the catalog-verified Kéire Hub 0.4.2 installer for supported Windows systems when active." active="downloads">
    <section class="platform-section"><div class="platform-shell product-details"><article class="prose"><p class="eyebrow">Windows 10 + 11 · x86-64</p><h1>Install Kéire through Hub.</h1><p class="lead">Kéire Hub 0.4.2 is the current Windows publication target. Until sequence 17 activates, the link remains the separately active 0.4.1 catalog release. Every download appears only from an unexpired signed catalog record, and its artifact SHA-256 remains visible before installation.</p><div class="download-card notice-panel" data-platform="windows"><p data-download-state>Checking the active signed catalog for Windows…</p><div class="download-variants" data-download-variants></div></div><p>The Ed25519-signed Kéire catalog verifies release metadata and the complete installer hash. The current EXE is not Authenticode-signed, so Windows may display an unknown-publisher warning. Verify the displayed SHA-256 before running it.</p><aside class="notice-panel"><strong>Updating from Hub 0.4.1</strong><p>The 0.4.1 in-app updater requires an Authenticode signature and cannot launch the unsigned 0.4.2 installer. When 0.4.2 becomes active, download and run it manually unless the release publishes a signed bridge build.</p></aside><h2>What Hub installs</h2><p>Hub remains separate from Editors and projects. It manages versioned Editor installations, compatible Build Support, templates, package tasks, and project launch.</p></article><aside><dl class="fact-list"><div><dt>Release target</dt><dd>0.4.2</dd></div><div><dt>Architecture</dt><dd>x86-64</dd></div><div><dt>OS</dt><dd>Windows 10 or 11</dd></div><div><dt>Availability</dt><dd>Signed catalog controlled</dd></div><div><dt>Integrity</dt><dd>Signed catalog + SHA-256 required</dd></div><div><dt>Native signing</dt><dd>Not Authenticode-signed</dd></div></dl></aside></div></section>
</PlatformLayout>
<script src="/assets/downloads.js" defer></script>
